    "created_at": "2023-10-25T17:10:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-25T17:10:56Z",
    "body": "> Does it also give a way of determining the semantics, in terms of base text and mapping of base text segments to annotation segments?\r\n\r\nIt doesn't define the semantics, but it does have a mapping algorithm in https://www.w3.org/TR/css-ruby-1/#ruby-pairing ...\r\n\r\nI agree with @domenic that the HTML spec should continue to say what ruby markup represents, and defining the mapping of ruby annotations to their bases is a core part of defining what it means. Ruby markup isn't always represented using CSS ruby layout, but however it's presented, that mapping is fundamental to what ruby is and how it should be interpreted.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
